== Chapter X

#block(inset: (x: 1em))[
  #set par(justify: false)
  #text(size: 0.9em)[#emph[The Second particular Direction. Get a clear Sense of] (1) #emph[The Guilt of the Sin perplexing. Considerations for Help therein proposed.] (2) #emph[The Danger manifold]: 1. #emph[Hardening.] 2. #emph[Temporal Correction.] 3. #emph[Loss of Peace and Strength.] 4. #emph[Eternal Destruction. Rules for this Management of the Consideration.] (3) #emph[The Evil of it]: 1. #emph[In Grieving the Spirit.] 2. #emph[Wounding the New Creature.]]
]

==== Second Direction: A Clear Sense of the Guilt, Danger, and Evil of the Sin

#smallcaps[THE] #emph[Second Direction] is this, #emph[Get a clear and abiding Sense upon thy Mind and Conscience] of the (1) #emph[Guilt,] (2) #emph[Danger,] (3) #emph[Evil] of that Sin wherewith thou art perplexed.

(1) Of the #emph[Guilt] of it. It is one of the #emph[Deceits] of a #emph[prevailing] Lust, to extenuate its own Guilt. Is it not a little one? When I go and #emph[bow myself in the House of Rimmon,] God be #emph[merciful] to me in This thing. #emph[Though this be bad,] yet it is not so bad as such and such an Evil, others of the People of God have had such a Frame; yea what dreadful Actual sins have some of them fallen into! Innumerable ways there are whereby Sin diverts the #emph[Mind] from a right and due Apprehension of its Guilt. Its noisome Exhalations #emph[darken] the Mind, that it cannot make a right Judgment of things; Perplexing Reasonings, extenuating Promises, tumultuating Desires, treacherous Purposes of relinquishment, hopes of Mercy; all have a share in disturbing the Mind, in its Consideration of the Guilt of a prevailing Lust. The #emph[Prophet] tells us, that Lust will do thus #emph[wholly,] when it comes to the height: Hos 4:11. #emph[Whoredom and Wine and new Wine take away the heart]: The #emph[Heart,] (i.e.) the #emph[understanding,] as it is often used in the Scripture. And as they accomplish this work to the #emph[height] in #emph[unregenerate Persons,] so in part in #emph[regenerate] also. #emph[Solomon] tells you of him who was #emph[enticed] by the #emph[lewd Woman,] that he was among the #emph[simple ones,] he was a #emph[young man void of understanding,] Prov 7:7. And wherein did his #emph[folly] appear? Why says he, in the 23d verse. #emph[He knew not that it was for his Life]\; He #emph[considered] not the #emph[Guilt] of the Evil that he was #emph[involved] in. And the Lord rendering a #emph[Reason] why his dealings with #emph[Ephraim] took no better Effect, gives this Account: #emph[Ephraim is like a silly Dove without heart,] Hos 7:11 had no understanding of his #emph[own miserable] Condition. Had it been possible that #emph[David] should have lain so long in the Guilt of that abominable Sin, but that he had #emph[innumerable] corrupt Reasonings, hindering him from taking a clear View of its Ugliness and Guilt in the Glass of the Law? This made the #emph[Prophet] that was sent for his awaking, in his dealings with him, to shut up all #emph[subterfuges] and Pretenses, by his Parable; that so he might fall fully under a sense of the Guilt of it. This is the #emph[proper] issue of Lust in the #emph[heart,] it darkens the Mind that it shall not #emph[judge] aright of its #emph[Guilt]\; And many other #emph[Ways] it hath for its own Extenuation, that I shall not now insist on. Let this then be the #emph[first care] of him that would #emph[mortify] Sin, to fix a #emph[right Judgment] of its #emph[Guilt] in his Mind. To which end take these Considerations to thy assistance:

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[1\. Though the Power of Sin be weakened by #emph[inherent] Grace in them that have it, that Sin shall not have #emph[dominion] over them, as it hath over others, yet the #emph[Guilt] of Sin that doth yet abide and remain, is aggravated and heightened by it, Rom 6:1, 2. #emph[What shall we say then? Shall we continue in Sin that Grace may abound? God forbid, how shall we that are dead to sin, live any longer therein?] How shall #emph[we] that are dead; the #emph[Emphasis] is on the word #emph[We.] How shall #emph[we] do it, who (as he afterwards describes it,) have received Grace from Christ to the contrary? We (doubtless) are more evil than any, if we do it. I shall not insist on the special Aggravations of the Sins of #emph[such] Persons; how they sin against more #emph[Love, Mercy, Grace, Assistance, Relief, Means] and #emph[Deliverances,] than others. But let this Consideration abide in thy Mind. There is inconceivably more Evil and Guilt in the #emph[Evil] of thy Heart, that doth remain, than there would be in so much Sin, if thou hadst no #emph[Grace] at all. Observe,]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[2\. That as God #emph[sees] abundance of #emph[beauty] and Excellency in the #emph[desires] of the Hearts of his Servants, more than in any the most #emph[glorious] works of other men, yea more than in most of their #emph[own] outward Performances, which have a greater mixture of Sin than the desires and Pantings of Grace in the Heart have: So God sees a #emph[great deal] of Evil in the #emph[working] of Lust in their Hearts, yea and more than in the #emph[open notorious Acts] of wicked men, or in many #emph[outward] Sins whereinto the #emph[Saints] may fall; seeing against them there is #emph[more Opposition] made, and more Humiliation generally follows them. Thus Christ, dealing with his decaying Children, goes to the root with them; lays aside their #emph[profession,] Rev 3:15. I know thee, thou art quite another thing than thou professest, and this makes thee abominable.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[So then; let these things and the like Considerations lead thee to a #emph[clear sense] of the Guilt of thy #emph[indwelling Lust,] that there may be no room in thy Heart for #emph[extenuating] or excusing thoughts, whereby Sin #emph[insensibly] will get #emph[strength] and prevail.]]

#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[(2) Consider the #emph[danger] of it, which is manifold:]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[1\. Of being #emph[hardened by its Deceitfulness:] This the Apostle sorely charges on the #emph[Hebrews,] ch. 3 vv. 12, 13. #emph[Take heed brethren, lest there be in any of you an evil heart of unbelief, in departing from the living God: But exhort one another daily, while it is called today, lest any of you be hardened through the deceitfulness of sin. Take heed] (saith he) use all #emph[means,] consider your #emph[Temptations, watch diligently,] there is a #emph[Treachery,] a #emph[deceit] in Sin, that tends to the #emph[hardening] of your Hearts from the Fear of God. The #emph[hardening] here mentioned is to the #emph[utmost; utter Obduration]\; Sin tends to it, and every #emph[Distemper] and Lust will make at least some progress towards it. Thou that wast #emph[tender,] and did'st use to #emph[melt] under the #emph[Word,] under #emph[Afflictions,] wilt grow (as some have #emph[profanely] spoken,) #emph[Sermon-proof,] and #emph[Sickness-proof]\; Thou that did'st #emph[tremble] at the #emph[presence] of God, thoughts of Death, and Appearance before him, when thou hadst more Assurance of his #emph[Love] than now thou hast, shalt have a Stoutness upon thy Spirit, not to be moved by these things. #emph[Thy Soul] and #emph[thy sin] shall be spoken of, and spoken to, and thou shalt not be at all #emph[concerned]\; But shalt be able to pass over Duties, Praying, Hearing, Reading, and thy Heart not in the least affected. Sin will #emph[grow] a #emph[light thing] to thee; thou wilt pass by it as a thing of nought; This it will grow to, and what will be the End of such a Condition? Can a sadder thing befall thee? Is it not enough to make any heart to tremble, to think of being brought into that Estate, wherein he should have #emph[slight] thoughts of Sin; slight thoughts of Grace, of Mercy, of the Blood of Christ, of the Law, Heaven and Hell, come all in at the same season? Take heed, this is that thy Lust is working towards; the #emph[hardening] of the Heart, #emph[searing] of Conscience, #emph[blinding] of the Mind, #emph[stupefying] of the Affections, and #emph[deceiving] of the whole Soul.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[2\. The #emph[danger] of some great #emph[temporal Correction,] which the Scripture calls #emph[Vengeance, Judgment,] and #emph[Punishment,] Ps 89:30, 31, 32, 33, Though God should not utterly #emph[cast] thee off for this #emph[Abomination] that lies in thy Heart, yet he will #emph[visit] with the #emph[Rod]\; though he pardon and forgive, he will take #emph[vengeance] of thy #emph[Inventions.] O remember #emph[David] and all his #emph[troubles]\; look on him #emph[flying] into the #emph[Wilderness,] and consider the hand of God upon him. Is it nothing to thee, that God should #emph[kill] thy #emph[Child] in #emph[anger, ruin] thy #emph[Estate] in #emph[anger,] break thy #emph[Bones] in #emph[anger,] suffer thee to be a Scandal and Reproach in #emph[anger,] kill thee, destroy thee, make thee lie down in #emph[darkness] in #emph[anger?] Is it nothing that he should #emph[punish, ruin,] and #emph[undo] others for thy sake? Let me not be mistaken, I do not mean, that God doth send all these things always on #emph[his] in Anger; God forbid. But this I say, That when he doth so deal with thee, and thy Conscience bears witness with him, what thy Provocations have been, thou wilt find his dealings full of #emph[bitterness] to thy Soul. If thou #emph[fearest] not these things, I #emph[fear] thou art under #emph[hardness.]]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[3\. #emph[Loss of Peace] and Strength all a mans days. To have #emph[peace] with God, to have strength to walk before God, is the #emph[sum] of the great #emph[Promises] of the #emph[Covenant] of Grace. In #emph[these] things is the #emph[Life] of our Souls. Without them in some #emph[comfortable] measure, to Live, is to Die. What good will our Lives do us, if we see not the #emph[face] of God sometimes in #emph[peace?] If we have not some strength to walk with him? Now both these will an #emph[unmortified Lust] certainly deprive the #emph[Souls] of men of. This #emph[case] is so evident in #emph[David,] as that nothing can be more clear. How often doth he complain that his #emph[bones] were broken, his #emph[Soul] disquieted, his wounds grievous on this account? Take other Instances, Isa 57:17. #emph[For the Iniquity of his Covetousness I was wroth, and hid myself.] What #emph[peace] I pray is there to a #emph[Soul] while God #emph[hides] himself? Or #emph[strength] whilst he #emph[smites?] Hos 5:15. #emph[I will go and return to my place, until they acknowledge their Offense, and seek my face.] I will #emph[leave] them, #emph[hide] my Face, and what will become of their #emph[peace] and #emph[strength?] If ever then thou hast enjoyed #emph[peace] with God, if ever his Terrors have made thee #emph[afraid,] if ever thou hast had #emph[strength] to walk with him, or ever hast #emph[mourned] in thy Prayer, and been troubled because of thy weakness, think of this danger that hangs over thy head. It is perhaps but a #emph[little] while and thou shalt see the Face of God in Peace no more: Perhaps by to #emph[morrow] thou shalt not be #emph[able] to #emph[pray, read, hear,] or perform any Duties with the least #emph[cheerfulness,] Life or Vigor; and possibly thou mayst never see a #emph[quiet] hour whilst thou livest; That thou mayst carry about thee #emph[broken bones] full of #emph[pain] and #emph[terror] all the days of thy Life; yea perhaps God will #emph[shoot] his Arrows at thee, and fill thee with Anguish and disquietness, with #emph[Fears] and #emph[Perplexities,] make thee a Terror and an Astonishment to thyself and others, show thee #emph[Hell] and Wrath every moment; frighten and scare thee with #emph[sad Apprehensions] of his Hatred, so that thy #emph[sore] shall run in the #emph[Night] season, and thy #emph[Soul] shall refuse #emph[Comfort]\; so that thou shalt #emph[wish Death] rather than #emph[Life,] yea thy Soul may #emph[choose strangling.] Consider this a little, though God should not #emph[utterly] destroy #emph[thee,] yet he #emph[might cast] thee into this #emph[condition,] wherein thou shalt have #emph[quick] and living Apprehensions of thy Destruction. #emph[Wont] thy Heart to thoughts hereof: Let it know what is like to be the #emph[Issue] of its State, leave not this #emph[Consideration] until thou hast made thy Soul to tremble within thee.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[4\. There is the Danger of #emph[eternal Destruction.] For the due Management of this Consideration, observe,]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[I. That there is such a #emph[connection] between a Continuance in Sin and #emph[eternal Destruction,] that though God does resolve to deliver some from a #emph[Continuance] in Sin, that they may not be destroyed, yet he will deliver none from Destruction that #emph[continue] in sin. So that whilst any one lies under an Abiding power of sin, the Threats of Destruction and everlasting #emph[Separation] from God are to be #emph[held] out to him: So Heb 3:12 to which add Heb 10:38. This is the Rule of Gods proceeding: If #emph[any] man #emph[depart] from him, #emph[draw back] through Unbelief, Gods Soul hath no pleasure in him; that is, his Indignation shall #emph[pursue] him to Destruction; so evidently, Gal 6:8.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[II. That he who is #emph[so entangled] (as above described) under the Power of any Corruption, can have at that present no clear prevailing Evidence of his #emph[Interest] in the Covenant, by the Efficacy whereof he may be delivered from Fear of Destruction. So that #emph[Destruction from the Lord] may justly be a Terror to him; And he may, he ought to look upon it, as that which will be the End of his #emph[Course] and ways. #emph[There is no condemnation to them that are in Christ Jesus,] Rom 8:1. #emph[True]! But who shall have the comfort of this Assertion? Who may #emph[assume] it to himself? #emph[They that walk after the Spirit, and not after the Flesh.] But you will say, Is not this to persuade men to #emph[unbelief?] I answer, No; there is a #emph[twofold Judgment] that a man may make of himself; 1. Of his #emph[Person,] and 2. Of his #emph[Ways.] It is the judgment of his #emph[Ways,] not his #emph[Person] that I speak of; Let a man get the best #emph[Evidence] for his #emph[Person] that he can, yet to judge that an evil #emph[Way] will end in Destruction, is his Duty; not to do it, is #emph[Atheism.] I do not say, that in such a Condition a man ought to throw away the Evidences of his personal Interest in Christ; but I say, he #emph[cannot keep] them. There is a two-fold #emph[condemnation] of a #emph[mans self]:]]

#pad(left: 4.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[First, In respect of #emph[Desert,] when the Soul concludes, that it Deserves to be cast out of the presence of God; and this is so far from a business of #emph[Unbelief,] that it is an Effect of Faith.]]

#pad(left: 4.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[Secondly, With respect to the #emph[Issue] and Event; when the Soul concludes it shall be Damned. I do not say this is the #emph[Duty] of any one, nor do I call them to it. But this I say, that the End of the way wherein a man is, ought by him to be concluded to be #emph[death,] that he may be provoked to fly #emph[from] it; And this is another #emph[Consideration,] that ought to #emph[dwell] upon such a Soul, if it desire to be #emph[freed] from the entanglement of its Lusts.]]

#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[(3) Consider the #emph[Evils] of it. I mean its #emph[present Evils.] Danger respects what is to come; Evil what is #emph[present:] Some of the many #emph[Evils] that attend an #emph[unmortified] Lust, may be mentioned.]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[1\. It #emph[grieves] the Holy and Blessed #emph[Spirit,] which is given to Believers to #emph[dwell in them] and #emph[abide] with them. So the Apostle, (Eph 4:25, 26, 27, 28, 29) dehorting them from many #emph[Lusts] and Sins, gives this as the great #emph[Motive] of it, v. 30. #emph[Grieve not the Holy Spirit, whereby you are sealed to the day of Redemption. Grieve] not that #emph[Spirit] of God (saith he) whereby you receive #emph[so many] and #emph[so great] Benefits; of which he instances in one #emph[signal] and #emph[comprehensive] one, #emph[Sealing to the day of Redemption.] He is #emph[grieved] by it, as a tender and #emph[loving Friend] is grieved at the #emph[unkindness] of his Friend, of whom he hath well deserved; so is it with this #emph[tender] and loving Spirit, who hath chosen our Hearts for an Habitation to #emph[dwell in,] and there to do for us all that our Souls desire. He is grieved by our harboring his #emph[Enemies,] and those whom he is to destroy in our Hearts with him. He doth not #emph[afflict] willingly, nor grieve Us, Lam 3:33 and shall we daily #emph[grieve] Him? Thus is he said sometimes to be #emph[vexed,] sometimes #emph[grieved at his heart,] to #emph[express] the greatest sense of our #emph[provocation.] Now if there be any thing of #emph[gracious Ingenuity] left in the Soul, if it be not utterly hardened by the Deceitfulness of Sin, this Consideration will #emph[certainly] affect it. Consider Who and What #emph[thou art, who] the #emph[Spirit] is that is #emph[grieved, what] he hath #emph[done] for thee, #emph[what] he comes to thy Soul #emph[about, what] he hath already done #emph[in thee]\; and be #emph[ashamed.] Among those who walk with God, there is no greater Motive and #emph[Incentive] unto universal Holiness, and the preserving of their Hearts and Spirits in all Purity and Cleanness, than this, That the blessed Spirit who hath undertaken to #emph[dwell] in them as Temples of God, and to preserve them meet for him who so #emph[dwells] in them, is continually considering what they give Entertainment in their Hearts unto; and rejoiceth when his #emph[Temple] is kept #emph[undefiled]\; that was an high Aggravation of the Sin of #emph[Zimri,] that he brought his #emph[Adulteress] into the Congregation in the sight of #emph[Moses,] and the rest, who were weeping for the Sins of the people, Num 25:6 and is it not an high Aggravation of the countenancing a Lust, or suffering it to abide in the Heart, when it is (as it must be, if we are Believers) entertained under the #emph[peculiar] Eye and View of the Holy Ghost; taking care to preserve his Tabernacle pure and holy?]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[2\. The #emph[Lord Jesus] is #emph[wounded] afresh by it; His #emph[new Creature] in the #emph[heart] is wounded. His Love is foiled, his #emph[adversary] gratified. As a total #emph[relinquishment] of him by the Deceitfulness of Sin, is the crucifying him afresh, and #emph[the putting of him to open shame,] so every #emph[harboring] of Sin that he came to destroy, wounds and grieves him.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[3\. It will #emph[take away] a mans #emph[usefulness] in his Generation. His Works, his #emph[Endeavors,] his #emph[Labors] seldom receive Blessing from God. If he be a #emph[Preacher,] God commonly #emph[blows] upon his #emph[Ministry,] that he shall #emph[labor] in the Fire, and not be #emph[honored] with any success, or doing any work for God; and the like may be spoken of other Conditions. The world is at this day full of poor #emph[withering] Professors; how few are there that walk in any Beauty, or Glory; how #emph[barren,] how useless are they for the most part! Amongst the many #emph[Reasons] that may be assigned of this sad Estate, it may justly be feared, that this is none of the least effectual; many men harbor Spirit-devouring Lusts in their bosoms, that lie as Worms at the Root of their Obedience, and #emph[corrode] and weaken it day by day. All Graces, all the Ways and Means whereby any Graces may be exercised and improved, are prejudiced by this Means; and as to any success, God blasts such men's undertakings.]]

#pad(left: 2.0em)[#par(first-line-indent: (amount: 12pt, all: true))[This then is my #emph[second Direction,] and it regards the Opposition that is to be made to #emph[Lust,] in respect of its habitual #emph[residence] in the Soul; keep alive upon thy Heart these or the #emph[like Considerations,] of its #emph[Guilt, Danger] and #emph[Evil]\; be much in the #emph[meditation] of these things; cause thy Heart to dwell and abide upon them. #emph[Engage] thy Thoughts into these Considerations; let them not #emph[go off,] nor wander from them, until they begin to have a powerful Influence upon thy #emph[Soul]\; until they make it to #emph[tremble.]]]
